{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rq/rq/pulls/2515","id":4723762028,"node_id":"PR_kwDOACpKWM8AAAABGY7jbA","html_url":"https://github.com/rq/rq/pull/2515","diff_url":"https://github.com/rq/rq/pull/2515.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/rq/rq/pull/2515.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rq/rq/issues/2515","number":2515,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"Preserve dependent jobs from one-shot enqueue_many iterables","user":{"login":"liuyinchu","id":206072046,"node_id":"U_kgDODEho7g","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/206072046?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/liuyinchu","html_url":"https://github.com/liuyinchu","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/liuyinchu/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/liuyinchu/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/liuyinchu/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/liuyinchu/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/liuyinchu/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/liuyinchu/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/liuyinchu/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/liuyinchu/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/liuyinchu/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"`Queue.enqueue_many()` accepts `Iterable[EnqueueData]`, but filters that iterable twice. The first traversal exhausts generators and other one-shot inputs, so jobs with dependencies disappear from the second batch. A generator containing two jobs depending on a queued parent returns `[]`, with neither child saved in Redis. The equivalent list returns two deferred jobs.\n\nPartition the input in one pass into the existing independent/dependent batches. This preserves the current independent/unmet/met return ordering, queue ordering, and pipeline execution points without making an additional full copy of the input. Update the parameter docstring to match the existing `Iterable` annotation.\n\nRegression coverage is a single focused generator test with one dependent and one independent job. It checks that both jobs are returned, the independent job is queued, and the dependent job is persisted as deferred and appears in the deferred registry. Existing pipeline tests are unchanged.\n\n## Validation\n\nFor the simplified test revision:\n\n- Focused enqueue-many tests: 3 passed\n- Queue, dependency, job-dependency, and group suites with slow tests enabled: 120 passed (13 fork-related deprecation warnings)\n- Full-source/test Ruff, changed-file formatting, and `git diff --check`: passed\n- The new regression fails against the pre-fix parent (`8fe33aa`): only the independent job is returned. It passes with the existing production fix.\n\nTested on Linux x86_64 / Python 3.12.14 / Redis 7.4.2 / redis-py 8.1.0. The full suite, other client/server versions, type checking, and builds were not rerun for this tests-only revision.\n\n### Historical validation before test simplification (`ca4a6e5`)\n\n- Focused enqueue-many tests: 4 passed, 12 subtests passed\n- Full suite with slow tests enabled: 748 passed, 1 SSL test skipped, 12 subtests passed (260 warnings)\n- Queue, dependency, job-dependency, and group suites: 121 passed, 12 subtests passed with both redis-py 8.1.0 and 5.0.1\n- Full-source/test Ruff, changed-file formatting, mypy (45 source files), and source/wheel builds pass\n- Independent differential review: 540 comparisons with original list behavior passed across six iterable types and internal/caller pipelines\n\nThe earlier expanded regressions failed against the original source in the three expected generator-loss cases. Tested on Linux x86_64 / Python 3.12.14 / Redis 7.4.2. SSL, Valkey, other Redis server versions and the full Python/platform matrix were not run.\n\nAI assistance: OpenAI Codex generated the patch and tests and performed the local validation. A second Codex reviewer independently checked the implementation and differential behavior. This draft does not imply human review or maintainer acceptance.\n\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->\n## Summary by CodeRabbit\n\n* **Bug Fixes**\n  * Fixed bulk job enqueueing to handle one-shot iterables, such as generators, without losing jobs that have dependencies or jobs that can be queued immediately.\n  * Dependent jobs are deferred and registered correctly, while independent jobs are queued as expected.\n  * The returned job order and queue contents remain correct when bulk enqueueing from a generator.\n<!-- end of auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->","created_at":"2026-10-03T03:29:16Z","updated_at":"2026-10-11T00:35:14Z","closed_at":"2026-10-10T14:49:01Z","merged_at":"2026-10-10T14:49:01Z","merge_commit_sha":"f114a649c57555bed3100b7b1e00fb8996d5d1d5","assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[],"labels":[],"milestone":null,"draft":false,"commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rq/rq/pulls/2515/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rq/rq/pulls/2515/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rq/rq/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rq/rq/issues/2515/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rq/rq/statuses/f7d1c7a121b7f110517803ea14ede6b01694f5d1","head":{"label":"liuyinchu:fix/enqueue-many-one-shot-iterables","ref":"fix/enqueue-many-one-shot-iterables","sha":"f7d1c7a121b7f110517803ea14ede6b01694f5d1","user":{"login":"liuyinchu","id":206072046,"node_id":"U_kgDODEho7g","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/206072046?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/liuyinchu","html_url":"https://github.com/liuyinchu","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/liuyinchu/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/liuyinchu/following{/other_user}","gists_url